{title: To the End of the Age}
{subtitle: Matthew 28:16–20}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 129}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Ab] |
| [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Eleven men went to Gali[Bb]lee, up the mountain path
[Cm]Where the risen Lord had told them that they'd [Ab]see his face at last
When they [Eb]saw him they worshiped him, though [Bb]some of them still doubted
[Cm]And Jesus came and spoke to them, and the [Ab]hills around them sounded
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Cm]All authority in heaven and on [Ab]earth
Has been given to me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Therefore go and make disci[Bb]ples of all nations
Baptiz[Cm]ing them in the name of the Father and of [Ab]the Son and of the Holy [Bb]Spirit
Teaching [Eb]them to keep everything I have command[Bb]ed you
And remember, I am [Cm]with you always, to [Ab]the very end [Bb]of the [Eb]age
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Not just the strong and not just sure, [Bb]he sent the ones who doubted
[Cm]Fishermen and tax collectors, [Ab]all the ones he'd counted
From the [Eb]mountain into every town, [Bb]to every land and nation
[Cm]The word goes out from Galilee [Ab]to every generation
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
All [Cm]authority in heaven and on [Ab]earth
Has been given to me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Therefore go and make disci[Bb]ples of all nations
Baptizing [Cm]them in the name of the Father and of the [Ab]Son and of the Holy Spirit
[Bb]Teaching them to [Eb]keep everything I have commanded [Bb]you
And remember, I [Cm]am with you always, to [Ab]the very end [Bb]of the [Eb]age
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Ab] | [Bb] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]I am with you al[Bb]ways
I am with you al[Cm][Ab]ways [Bb][Eb]
To the [Bb]very end [Cm]of [Eb]the age
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Go and make disciples [Bb]of all nations [Cm][Ab][Bb]
[Eb]I am with you al[Bb][Cm][Ab][Bb][Eb]ways
{end_of_verse}
